r allows it.\n\nP2-2. .claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:376 (_E4_POSTURE_TOGGLE_SCRIPTS) together with .claude/hooks/_lib/_night_mode_parts/toggles.py\n- Scenario: the code that writes the posture now lives in an importable module. A model-rail `python3 -c` body can put .claude/hooks on sys.path, call _night_mode_parts.install() on a namespace it builds itself, and call cmd_on(). It names neither .claude/scripts/night-mode.py nor settings.local.json, so neither the _e4 matcher nor the _e3 literal scan sees it, and main()'s NF-08b check never runs.\n- This is the same class as the Python-level string-concatenation bypass that already exists (runpy on a split path), so it is not a new capability. Still, the table's own comment says every future posture writer must be registered there.\n- Minimal fix: treat the module as a writer by matching `_night_mode_parts` in -c bodies, or move the CI refusal and the self-path guard into cmd_on, cmd_off and cmd_off_discard_snapshot so that calling them through the parts also refuses.\n\nP2-3. .claude/scripts/night-mode.py:326-331 (the parts import now runs at load time, before _check_self_path at :518)\n- Scenario: a copy moved outside any repo tree (for example /tmp/a/b/c/night-mode.py) now dies with an ImportError traceback and exit 1. Before, it refused with exit 2 plus the summary line. It still writes nothing.\n- The docstring (\"2 — ... alias/relocated invocation (NF-08b)\") and the CHANGELOG line \"Entry points keep ... their observable contracts\" no longer hold for this edge case.\n- Minimal fix: wrap the import in try/except ImportError and exit 2 with an NF-08b message.\n\nP2-4. .claude/scripts/reality-ledger.py:81-83\n- Scenario: the parts import sits outside the FATAL ImportError block at :58-69. A broken or missing parts package exits 1 with a traceback, not the documented \"2 = detector internal error\".\n- Minimal fix: move the import and the install() call inside that try.\n\nP2-5. .claude/hooks/_lib/_profile_opus_parts/latency.py:119-127 (carried, moved word for word, not introduced by this delta)\n- Scenario: the isolation scrub drops CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR_NATIVE but not CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH, and CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH outranks CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR (_audit_log_parts/paths_skills.py:10).\n- A maintainer who runs --hook-latency with CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH exported appends about 1,000 or more measured hook rows to the live HMAC chain. That breaks the docstring promise \"never the real ~/.claude\" and is the same class as the diagnose-output-hook P1 cured in v1.4.3-rc.1.\n- Minimal fix: add CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH and the other location variables that diagnose-output-hook.py strips to the scrub tuple.\n\nP2-6. Housekeeping\n- .github/CODEOWNERS:122 still names only .claude/scripts/profile-opus-4-7.py. Its logic now lives in .claude/hooks/_lib/_profile_opus_parts/; add an entry if per-file ownership is intended.\n- The night-mode.py:320-324 header comment (\"Path resolution — anchored in FUNCTIONS\") now introduces an import block; update it.\n\nVERDICT: GO In this payload the four script splits keep behavior and the fail direction intact, the parts ship to installs, condition 7 and the pin facts behind condition 9 hold against the code, and what I found is P2 only: the re-pin generator mislabels a floor-to-bounded change as a widening, and there are minor gaps in exit-code contracts and isolation.\n","numLines":55,"startLine":1,"totalLines":55}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Am5mdk9er4CyydPrFEuVJ2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
