{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WfPq58XZPpwunF6TPs6q13","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tPAYLOAD 30/32 — v1.4.3-rc.1..0e687e3c5285. I read every hunk against the redacted candidate tree.\n2\t\n3\tSCOPE OF THIS PAYLOAD\n4\t.claude/scripts/{context-budget.py, derive-audit-family.py, diagnose-output-hook.py, env-inventory.json, gen-command-skill-hook-map.py, generate-available-models.py, lessons.py, model-deprecations.json}, plus .claude/scripts/local/{_release_bump_sites.py, mac_sign_and_release.py (new), pair-rail-gate.sh, release.sh}.\n5\t\n6\tDECLARED CONDITIONS TOUCHED HERE (all hold against the code)\n7\t- Cond. 3(a) holds. diagnose-output-hook.py:27-48 removes HOME, CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH/ERR/LOCK/KEY_PATH/LAST_HMAC_PATH/CHAIN_LENGTH_PATH/FALLBACK_PATH/ROTATE_BYTES/HMAC_DISABLE and CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR_NATIVE from the child environment. It then sets HOME=tmp, CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR=tmp/audit and CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR=tmp/state. The list matches _lib/test_isolation.py exactly: ALL_AUDIT_CARRIERS plus WHOLE_DIR_OVERRIDE_CARRIERS. spool_writer and _audit_emit_parts/writer.py read only carriers that are in this list.\n8\t- Cond. 12 holds. The pattern at _release_bump_sites.py:90, ((?:--pin |git tag --list ['\"]?)v)SEMVER, has one capture group, and _plain_replacement rebuilds it as \\g<1>+target. It matches exactly the three example lines at INSTALL.md:717/719/722. The `--pin \"$(git tag` prefix on line 717 does not match `--pin v`, so it is not touched. INSTALL.md warns about the `unknown --pin ref` failure, as declared. upgrade.sh is withheld, so I could not check exit code 2 from this tree.\n9\t- Cond. 7 holds. context-budget.py and lessons.py keep their paths; the logic moves to _lib/_context_budget_parts and _lib/_lessons_parts.\n10\t- Cond. 9 and 10 hold. generate-available-models.py adds the model_currency family prefixes once the ADR-149 policy fence is present. pair-rail-gate.sh Gate 4 now accepts a JSON status of `compatible` next to `verified`; anything else after rc=0 fails closed. The compatible arm reads the version from package.json and never runs the binary, so M4 ordering (verify before any exec) is kept. Both changes are the declared family/version-floor behavior.\n11\t\n12\tMOVED-CODE CHECKS (no defect found)\n13\t- Binding: context-budget and lessons rebuild every exported function on the facade globals. That keeps monkeypatch points, `__file__` lookups (so lessons `_load_injection_scanner` still resolves .claude/scripts/scan-injection.py), and the `_rp`/`FileLock`/`Lesson`/`_FILELOCK_AVAILABLE` lookups.\n14\t- Name coverage: every name of the old lessons.py and context-budget.py appears in some part's `__all__`.\n15\t- Import order: the part modules have no import-time dependency on facade names. inventory.py duplicates CHARS_PER_TOKEN and REDACTED for HONESTY_NOTES with the same values, and render.py imports the defaults from .config. `_sanitize_one_liner`'s default binds at definition time, as before.\n16\t- `__annotations__`: lessons.py:208-209 drops the module annotations the binder creates when they are empty; install always creates them, so there is no NameError.\n17\t- Shipping and guarding: classes are rebuilt only for context-budget; the lessons parts define none. install.sh ships the new _lib/* subdirectories (the exclusion predicate skips only tests/test_isolation/testing/pycache). The parts fall under the canonical glob .claude/hooks/_lib/**/*.py, so canonical protection of lessons.py carries over.\n18\t- Hook impact: emit_architect_outcome.py imports lessons, which now also needs _lib._lessons_parts and _lib._audit_emit_parts. Both ship, and the failure class (missing _lib module at import) is the same as before.\n19\t- Python and dependencies: everything is standard library and Python 3.9 compatible (argparse `required=` exists since 3.7; FunctionType rebinding; no match statements or PEP 604 unions).\n20\t- Fail direction: no hook fail direction changes in this payload.\n21\t- Writes: nothing writes outside its place. The new maintainer script is not installed into adopter repos: install_scripts_selective copies only top-level .claude/scripts/*.\n22\t\n23\tP0\n24\tNone.\n25\t\n26\tNEW FINDINGS (annex)\n27\tNo undeclared P1 in this payload.\n28\t\n29\tP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n30\t1. .claude/hooks/_lib/_context_budget_parts/status.py:97-102 — wrong probe-status text. The D2 record (rendered by --json and --probe-status) still says \"removal_scope\": \"non-canonical, no ceremony: the D2 block in this file\". The D2 code now lives in _lib/_context_budget_parts/summarization.py, which the canonical guard covers via .claude/hooks/_lib/**/*.py. The old .claude/scripts/context-budget.py was not canonical (canonical_edit/guards.py lists no such path). So a maintainer who follows the ledger will hit the sentinel gate. Related: the context-budget.py docstring still says \"This file also carries three decision probes\". Fix: reword removal_scope to name the summarization.py part and the canonical sentinel, and update the facade docstring. More generally, cond. 7 / the CHANGELOG do not say that script logic moved under _lib/** (context-budget, budget-summary, ceo-boot, audit-query, reality-ledger, profile-opus, …) is now sentinel-gated where the old script file was not. That is a tightening for adopters who patch these scripts, not a defect; worth one line in Known-open or in cond. 7.\n31\t2. .claude/scripts/local/mac_sign_and_release.py:130 — the wrapper always passes --npm-readme-reviewed to `release.sh bump`. It only prints a prerequisite and never asks for confirmation. release.sh:58-62/561-570 makes this flag a deliberate human attestation, because the npm/README `last-reviewed` stamp is a tripwire. The wrapper turns that attestation into boilerplate on material a signed tag covers. Related nits:\n32\t   - TRACK (line 16) and the \"Merge pull request #7\" message (line 113) are hard-coded.\n33\t   - sign-merge always pushes main (line 119) without a --push opt-in, unlike cut-rc/cut-ga, while release.sh's header promises it never pushes.\n34\t   Fix: require an explicit --npm-readme-reviewed (or an interactive confirmation) on the wrapper; parameterize the track and PR number; gate the main push behind --push.\n35\t3. .claude/scripts/gen-command-skill-hook-map.py:206-219 — the generator takes the package to scan from the import (`from _lib._audit_emit_parts import install`) and ignores the `package=` keyword. For check_agent_spawn.py (install(..., package=\"_lib.agent_spawn\")) it scans _audit_emit_parts/*.py instead of agent_spawn/*.py. This does not change today's doc, because the facade itself matches. Also, the emitted \"Derivation rule\" text (line 352) still says \"source file\" although bound parts now count, and the strict utf-8 read drops the old errors=\"replace\". Fix: when a Call node has a `package=` keyword, scan that package; update the rule text.\n36\t4. .claude/scripts/generate-available-models.py:2-31 and 47-51 — the docstring still says \"Single source: the … block inside ADR-149\" and \"byte-deterministic … ADR order\". Under the policy fence, the output adds model_currency._PREFIXES. If that import fails with ImportError, the lambda fallback silently emits the bare ADR list. Fix: update the docstring; when the fence is present and the import fails, exit 2.\n37\t5. .claude/scripts/local/pair-rail-gate.sh:197 and :242 — stale comments. They still say \"0 = verified\" and \"reached ONLY after Gate 4 verified the payload sha\"; rc=0 now also covers `compatible`, which is not hash-verified. Fix: reword both comments.\n38\t6. .claude/scripts/local/_release_bump_sites.py:90 compared with verify-counts.sh:1099 — the writer now also rewrites the `git tag --list 'v…'` stem, but the oracle still watches only `--pin v`. That breaks the module's own \"anchored exactly as their oracle checks them\" claim, and a stale RC-resolution line would go undetected. Fix: widen the verify-counts INSTALL.md pattern to the same alternation.\n39\t7. .claude/scripts/model-deprecations.json:366-368 — rule `model-currency-family-prefixes` now exempts the whole of _lib/model_currency.py. Its reason text describes check-model-currency.py's prefix table, not model_currency.py's literal _RETIRED/_LEGACY_* id sets. Fix: give model_currency.py its own rule with an accurate reason, or narrow the exemption.\n40\t8. env-inventory.json — regenerated data. Two site counts went down (CEO_AUDIT_SYNC_MODE 9→8, CEO_WORKFLOW_LEDGER and CEO_WORKFLOW_RESUME_GUARD 7→6). I found no lost runtime read in this payload: spool_writer still owns CEO_AUDIT_SYNC_MODE. Worth confirming in the audit_emit split payload that no comment or read was intended there.\n41\t\n42\tVERDICT: GO The declared conditions this payload touches (3(a), 7, 9, 10, 12) all hold against the candidate tree, the context-budget and lessons facades keep their names, patch points and file-relative paths, and the only findings are maintainer-tooling and documentation P2s with no adopter-facing P0 or P1.\n43\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b6cbc95-c175-4ebd-a48b-61e9e70f7284","uuid":"f9190c13-f90f-4d9e-9362-8cc33ecede3f","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:06:07.789Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-30.verdict.txt","content":"PAYLOAD 30/32 — v1.4.3-rc.1..0e687e3c5285. I read every hunk against the redacted candidate tree.\n\nSCOPE OF THIS PAYLOAD\n.claude/scripts/{context-budget.py, derive-audit-family.py, diagnose-output-hook.py, env-inventory.json, gen-command-skill-hook-map.py, generate-available-models.py, lessons.py, model-deprecations.json}, plus .claude/scripts/local/{_release_bump_sites.py, mac_sign_and_release.py (new), pair-rail-gate.sh, release.sh}.\n\nDECLARED CONDITIONS TOUCHED HERE (all hold against the code)\n- Cond. 3(a) holds. diagnose-output-hook.py:27-48