{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PDrHrsarfn8mnx46HaVUPB","type":"tool_result","content":"490\t# match NOTHING and the gate would pass VACUOUSLY — silently stopping the\n491\t# drift check exactly when it matters most.\n492\t#\n493\t# IDEMPOTENCE (F2, the v1.3.0-rc.1 re-pass). A bump on a tree that is already\n494\t# at the target must write NOTHING — not one byte, not one index entry. It\n495\t# used to re-date four `last-reviewed:` stamps with today date, which on D+1\n496\t# of the ADR-103 hold produced a dirty tree, then a commit made AFTER the\n497\t# preflight proved CI green, which `tag()` then signed. That commit was also\n498\t# invisible to the pair-rail step 15 (none of the four files is in\n499\t# `pair-rail-inputs-hash-manifest.txt`). Two independent defenses now:\n500\t#   1. the same-tree predicate below (four oracles) short-circuits the phase;\n501\t#   2. the writer skips each stamp line whose version is already the target.\n502\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n503\t_oracle() {\n504\t  label=\"$1\"; shift\n505\t  if \"$@\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n506\t    printf '  --   oracle %s: PASS  (%s)\\n' \"$label\" \"$*\"\n507\t    return 0\n508\t  fi\n509\t  printf '  --   oracle %s: RED   (%s)\\n' \"$label\" \"$*\"\n510\t  return 1\n511\t}\n512\t\n513\t# All four are required. The fourth is not redundant: it is the ONLY watcher\n514\t# of the SBOM/SECURITY/VERSIONING stamps, which are outside the VERSION_SITES\n515\t# of verify-counts. Without it an external no-op would block the in-loop\n516\t# self-heal from ever running over a stale stamp. Freezing the DATE is safe\n517\t# because the freshness gate decides on the stamp VERSION, not its date.\n518\ttree_already_at_target() {\n519\t  cur_version=\"$(tr -d ' \\n' < VERSION)\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b6cbc95-c175-4ebd-a48b-61e9e70f7284","uuid":"aa668f2d-788f-47e2-ab68-c036a54bfb51","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:09:37.759Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/scripts/local/release.sh","content":"# match NOTHING and the gate would pass VACUOUSLY — silently stopping the\n# drift check exactly when it matters most.\n#\n# IDEMPOTENCE (F2, the v1.3.0-rc.1 re-pass). A bump on a tree that is already\n# at the target must write NOTHING — not one byte, not one index entry. It\n# used to re-date four `last-reviewed:` stamps with today date, which on D+1\n# of the ADR-103 hold produced a dirty tree, then a commit made AFTER the\n# preflight proved CI green, which `tag()` then signed. That commit was also\n# invisible to the pair-rail step 15 (none of the four files is in\n# `pair-rail-inputs-hash-manifest.txt`). Two independent defenses now:\n#   1. the same-tree predicate below (four oracles) short-circuits the phase;\n#   2. the writer skips each stamp line whose version is already the target.\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n_oracle() {\n  label=\"$1\"; shift\n  if \"$@\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    printf '  --   oracle %s: PASS  (%s)\\n' \"$label\" \"$*\"\n    return 0\n  fi\n  printf '  --   oracle %s: RED   (%s)\\n' \"$label\" \"$*\"\n  return 1\n}\n\n# All four are required. The fourth is not redundant: it is the ONLY watcher\n# of the SBOM/SECURITY/VERSIONING stamps, which are outside the VERSION_SITES\n# of verify-counts. Without it an external no-op would block the in-loop\n# self-heal from ever running over a stale stamp. Freezing the DATE is safe\n# because the freshness gate decides on the stamp VERSION, not its date.\ntree_already_at_target() {\n  cur_version=\"$(tr -d ' \\n' < VERSION)\"","numLines":30,"startLine":490,"totalLines":747}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PDrHrsarfn8mnx46HaVUPB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
